  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats delivered a twenty-six song performance at the Mr. Smalls Theatre in Millvale, Pennsylvania, on May 8, 2019 [1][5]. This recording, captured by LMGBTapes, is the only available version of this specific show and features a matrix mix of the soundboard and audience microphones [1]. The setlist spans material from albums such as In League with Dragons, The Sunset Tree, and Heretic Pride [1]. Notable tracks include “Going to Kansas,” which had not been played in over 1,100 days, and “Going Invisible 2,” a rare performance [1]. The band also shared stories about the song “No Children” and their return to the venue [1]. Listeners have praised this recording for its clarity, noting that the band and audience are blended just right [3]. One attendee described the evening as a mix of new and old songs, impeccably performed for an appreciative crowd [4]. The recording is rated five out of five stars by three users [1]. It is the 277th show in the archive’s collection for the band, following a previous performance at the same venue the day before [5]. The uploader thanks the venue staff and band management for permission to record [1].",
